[{"timestamp": "2026-04-05T16:41:25Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "VOC?", "role": "attempt", "is_correct": false, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-05T16:41:26Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "EIC", "role": "attempt", "is_correct": false, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-05T16:41:43Z", "username": "మాन$", "text": "British EIC is correct", "role": "hint", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-05T16:41:56Z", "username": "మాन$", "text": "9. This represented a state that seemed modern in administration and terrifyingly efficient in war, yet still rested on older architectures of dynasty, hierarchy, and command. It is often retrospectively blurred into later catastrophes, though it deserves to be understood as a distinct expression of continental order before ideological rupture transformed the continent. It looked disciplined because it was. What is it?", "role": "hint", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-05T16:42:08Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "Nazis", "role": "attempt", "is_correct": false, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-05T16:42:16Z", "username": "Sayu Sekhar", "text": "japan?", "role": "attempt", "is_correct": false, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-05T16:42:41Z", "username": "మాन$", "text": "Technically German Empire is correct", "role": "hint", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-05T16:42:47Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "is the connect cracked yet?", "role": "attempt", "is_correct": true, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-05T16:43:03Z", "username": "మాन$", "text": "10. This survives most powerfully not through uninterrupted rule, but through symbolic stubbornness. It belonged to a sovereignty that became historically larger after losing political centrality, because later identity projects needed its memory more than its institutions. It is both artifact and inheritance. What is it?", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-05T16:43:17Z", "username": "మాन$", "text": "Do not worry about it now", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-05T16:43:18Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "Roman", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-05T16:43:36Z", "username": "Sayu Sekhar", "text": "greek 😅", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-05T16:43:43Z", "username": "Sidhesh K K", "text": "Brunei", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}]